      "text": "If things couldn’t get any crazier in the Pacific, Tropical Storm Co-May has made landfall directly over the city of Shanghai and is causing major freshwater flooding in Zhejiang Province, China. Over 280,000 people were reportedly evacuated from flood-prone areas. \n\nCo-May previously struck Luzon in the Philippines after briefly reaching Typhoon status, and the system has already claimed 26 lives.\n\n(Radar credit: cyclonicwx)",
